{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "class Mapping:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.forwardMap = {}  # Stores the pattern -> value mapping\n        self.mappedValues = set() # Stores values that have already been mapped to a pattern\n\n    def consistent(self, pattern: str, value: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the current pattern-value pair is consistent with existing mappings.\n        Ensures that a pattern maps to only one value and a value is mapped by only one pattern.\n        \"\"\"\n        if pattern in self.forwardMap:\n            # If pattern is already mapped, its current mapping must match the given value\n            return self.forwardMap[pattern] == value\n        else:\n            # If pattern is not mapped, the given value must not be already mapped to another pattern\n            return value not in self.mappedValues\n\n    def addMapping(self, pattern: str, value: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Adds a new pattern-value mapping to the internal structures.\n        Assumes consistency has already been verified by the 'consistent' method.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.forwardMap[pattern] = value\n        self.mappedValues.add(value)\n        return True\n\nclass IsSamePatterns:\n    def validateLength(self, patterns: list[str], sequence: list[str]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the lengths of the patterns and sequence arrays are equal.\n        \"\"\"\n        return len(patterns) == len(sequence)\n\n    def computeAndCompare(self, patterns: list[str], sequence: list[str]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iterates through the patterns and sequence, applying and validating mappings.\n        \"\"\"\n        mapping = Mapping()\n        for i in range(len(patterns)):\n            pattern_element = patterns[i]\n            sequence_element = sequence[i]\n\n            if not mapping.consistent(pattern_element, sequence_element):\n                return False # Inconsistency found, not a bijection\n\n            # If consistent and it's a new pattern, add the mapping\n            if pattern_element not in mapping.forwardMap:\n                mapping.addMapping(pattern_element, sequence_element)\n        \n        return True # All elements processed consistently, bijection holds\n\n    def is_samepatterns(self, patterns: list[str], sequence: list[str]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Orchestrates the validation of lengths and computation of mapping consistency.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self.validateLength(patterns, sequence):\n            return False\n        \n        return self.computeAndCompare(patterns, sequence)\n\ndef is_samepatterns(patterns, sequence) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether a sequence follows the given patterns array based on a one-to-one mapping.\n    \"\"\"\n    facade = IsSamePatterns()\n    return facade.is_samepatterns(patterns, sequence)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "def _all_divisible(tup, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in a tuple are divisible by k.\n    Returns True if all elements are divisible, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    for element in tup:\n        if element % k != 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef find_tuples(list_of_tuples, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples from a list where all elements are divisible by k.\n    Returns a new list containing only the matching tuples, preserving their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for tup in list_of_tuples:\n        if _all_divisible(tup, k):\n            result.append(tup)\n    return result"}
